WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:05.870
Hey guys, my name's Lewis, I'm 27 years old and I'm from Bavaria, Germany.
大家好，我叫刘易斯，今年27岁，来自德国巴伐利亚。

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:07.481
I'm a very sensitive person.
我是一个非常敏感的人。

00:00:07.481 --> 00:00:13.353
I dream too big and I feel too much and growing up it's been so easy to become emotionally closed off.
我的梦想很大，内心感受也很丰富，在成长过程中，我特别容易在情感上自我封闭。

00:00:13.353 --> 00:00:27.628
I often catch myself drifting into this kind of an numbness where I just feel I don't belong but Ted gave and still gives me the strength to keep fighting for that vulnerable part of myself even when it so often feels like a fight for a lost cause.
我经常发现自己陷入一种麻木状态，觉得自己与世隔绝，但泰德过去和现在都给了我力量，让我继续为自己脆弱的那一部分抗争，尽管这种抗争常常让人觉得是在做无用功。

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:30.910
I'll stay out here on this cold roof for a little longer.
我要在这个寒冷的屋顶上再呆一会儿。

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.149
And I cannot thank you guys enough for that.
我对此对你们感激不尽。

00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:41.609
I'm alone, I'll be soon in New York City when I see you.
我孤身一人，很快就会去纽约市见你们。

00:00:45.539 --> 00:00:53.299
Please permit me to tell you everything, York City.
请允许我把一切都告诉你，纽约城。

00:00:53.299 --> 00:00:57.859
Well, hello and welcome to another episode of How We Made Your Mother.
嗯，大家好，欢迎收看另一期的《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:00:57.859 --> 00:00:58.700
I'm Josh Radner.
我是乔什·拉德纳。

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.799
I played Ted Mosby on How I Met Your Mother.
我在《老爸老妈浪漫史》中饰演了泰德·莫斯比。

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:05.659
every single episode from 2005 to 2013.
2005年到2013年的每一集。

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:06.500
Is that right?
是这样吗？

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.319
Yeah.
对。

00:01:07.319 --> 00:01:08.159
No, 13, 13.
不对，13年，13年。

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:09.000
Damn it.
该死。

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.840
13, yeah.
13年，对。

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.359
And I am joined.
和我一起的还有。

00:01:11.359 --> 00:01:12.239
14, sorry, Josh.
14年，抱歉，乔什。

00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:13.159
It is definitely 14.
绝对是14年。

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:14.000
It was nine years.
那是九年。

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.840
Here we go.
开始吧。

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:15.680
Good start.
好的开始。

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.519
The great start.
完美的开始。

00:01:16.519 --> 00:01:17.359
Hi, Craig Thomas.
嗨，克雷格·托马斯。

00:01:17.359 --> 00:01:18.599
I'm joined by Craig Thomas.
我和克雷格·托马斯在一起。

00:01:18.599 --> 00:01:20.200
He co-created the show with Carter Bass.
他和卡特·贝斯共同创作了这部剧。

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.359
Hi, Craig.
嗨，克雷格。

00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:23.599
I'm disoriented but happy to be here.
我有点晕头转向，但很高兴能来到这里。

00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:26.000
I don't know what year it is.
我都不知道今年是哪一年了。

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:36.224
We are joined today by a ray of sunshine is illuminating this riverside studio space with us today.
今天和我们在一起的还有一位宛如阳光般耀眼的朋友，她为我们这个河畔录音室增添了无限光彩。

00:01:36.224 --> 00:01:49.134
We have the very wonderful, endlessly entertaining and fun and delightful Ashley Williams who played Victoria in 16 episodes.
我们邀请到了非常精彩、妙趣横生、幽默可爱阿什莉·威廉姆斯，她在16集中饰演了维多利亚。

00:01:49.134 --> 00:01:50.580
Is that right?
是这样吗？

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:51.561
I think that's correct.
我想是的。

00:01:51.561 --> 00:01:53.565
We can't count, but don't take our word for it.
我们不会数数，但别全信我们的话。

00:01:53.565 --> 00:01:55.400
We don't even know how many seasons we did.
我们甚至不知道自己拍了多少季。

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.799
This is not, we're not nailing the math this, I'm high, Ashley, hi, welcome.
这不是……我们在数学上没做好，嗨，阿什莉，嗨，欢迎。

00:01:58.799 --> 00:01:59.799
Hi, Josh.
嗨，乔什。

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:02.920
Hi, Craig, I'm so excited to be here.
嗨，克雷格，我很高兴能来到这里。

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:04.140
Thank you so much for having me.
非常感谢邀请我。

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.079
I love the podcast.
我很喜欢这个播客。

00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:07.079
Oh, thanks.
哦，谢谢。

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:11.719
Yeah, it's so cool to be now on a podcast that I'm genuinely a fan of.
耶，能来到一个我真心喜欢的播客节目，感觉太酷了。

00:02:11.719 --> 00:02:14.439
I'm really enjoying listening to the show.
我真的很享受听这个节目。

00:02:14.439 --> 00:02:15.960
So make us a quick commercial.
那给我们做一个简短的广告吧。

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.360
What do you love about our podcast?
你喜欢我们的播客什么？

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:22.199
And by the way, stealth FU to every other podcast you've ever been on.
顺便说一句，向你以前上过的所有其他播客隐秘地爆句粗口吧。

00:02:22.199 --> 00:02:23.447
You are the best.
你是最棒的。

00:02:23.447 --> 00:02:26.088
Ashley, she is the best of the best.
阿什莉，她真的是最棒中的最棒。

00:02:26.088 --> 00:02:34.451
The day is better when you see Ashley when you experience just being anywhere near her, even on a computer screen.
当你看到阿什莉时，当你体验到哪怕只是通过电脑屏幕和她待在附近时，这一天都会变得更美好。

00:02:34.451 --> 00:02:38.706
Thank you for being Victoria and thank you for being here.
谢谢你成为维多利亚，也谢谢你来到这里。

00:02:38.706 --> 00:02:40.319
We love you very much.
我们非常爱你。

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:41.553
I love you guys.
我也爱你们。

00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:47.720
I'm so happy it was a miraculous job back in the day and the dividends continue.
我太高兴了，当年这是一份奇迹般的工作，而且它的红利一直在延续。

00:02:47.719 --> 00:03:02.199
Actually, how do you, like, I know that was a Ted-centered testimonial from our friend in Bavaria, but what's that like when you hear these testimonials about what the show means to people and how invested they continue to be after so many years?
阿什莉，你觉得……我知道那是来自我们巴伐利亚朋友的以泰德为中心的感言，但是当你听到这些关于这部剧对人们意味着什么、以及在这么多年后他们依然投入其中有什么感想？

00:03:02.199 --> 00:03:19.719
You know what's so funny is like, you guys have said this before, and I know just from talking to you personally, like, at the time, you know, we were, Josh, like, we were newer actors in the industry, and I was like, like, oh my gosh, how did you get a pilot, Josh?
你知道最有趣的是什么吗，就像你们之前说过的那样，而且我知道仅仅通过和你们私下交流，当时，你知道的，乔什，就像，我们在行业里是更新的新人，当时我就想，哦天哪，乔什，你是怎么拿到试播集的？

00:03:19.719 --> 00:03:21.439
Like, how did you, you know what I mean?
就像，你是怎么……你知道我的意思吗？

00:03:21.439 --> 00:03:30.599
Like, that was the majority of our initial conversations when we first got to know each other was like, I can't believe you're on this show, I can't believe it's picked up for like 12.
刚认识的时候，我们最初的大部分对话都是这样的：我不敢相信你能演这部剧，我不敢相信它竟然续订了12集。

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:36.280
Well, do you remember, I don't know if you remember where I met you, we talked about this, but I don't think you'll remember.
好吧，你还记得吗，我不知道你是否记得我在哪里遇到你的，我们聊过这个，但我觉得你不会记得。

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.879
I went to a taping of Good Morning Miami because I was friends with Mark Foyerstein.
我去看过《晨安，迈阿密》的拍摄，因为我和马克·费尔施泰因是朋友。

00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:46.319
And I met you kind of briefly, But that's how I knew you, because you were on that show.
我算是在那之前简短地见过你，但我就是通过那样认识你的，因为你演了那部剧。

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:47.240
You remember that show.
你还记得那部剧。

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.960
That's fascinating.
真迷人。

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:56.479
I do remember that show, but what was really interesting about that show, that was my first TV job out of college.
我确实记得那部剧，但那部剧真正有趣的地方在于，那是我大学毕业后的第一份电视工作。

00:03:56.479 --> 00:03:58.719
I had only done a bunch of theater.
我之前只演过一堆戏剧。

00:03:58.719 --> 00:04:02.800
And Mark Feuerstein is one of the golden humans in my life.
马克·费尔施泰因是我生命中最金子般的人之一。

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.639
Shout out to Mark, yes.
向马克致敬，是的。

00:04:04.639 --> 00:04:06.159
Shout out to Mark.
向马克致敬。

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:27.947
And also it was an education in, You know, what I think is really common in sitcom culture, which is it's an incredibly competitive amongst the writers to make sure that people's jokes are getting in and tape night can go badly and tape night can go well and it's stressful and the ratings are up and down.
这也是一次教育，你知道的，我认为这在情景喜剧文化中非常普遍，那就是编剧之间的竞争极其激烈，他们要确保大家的笑话都能用上，录制之夜可能会很不顺，也可能会很顺利，压力很大，收视率起起伏伏。

00:04:27.947 --> 00:04:41.120
It's not, you know, I've now done a ton of different mediums in television and the multi-cam medium had been incredibly stressful medium for me to to be thrown into right out of school.
这并不是，你知道的，我现在在电视领域做过大量不同的媒介，而多机位媒介对我来说是一个极具压力的媒介，刚从学校出来就被扔进这个环境里。

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:47.800
So it's so interesting that you came to a tape of Good Morning Miami because they were incredibly stressful times for me.
所以你能来看《晨安，迈阿密》的录制真的很有趣，因为那对我来说是一段压力极大的时期。

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:53.160
And it's part of how when I first started on the show, I first got the job.
这也是我刚开始加入这部剧、刚得到这份工作时的一部分经历。

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.360
And I mean, I remember the audition so well, I remember booking it.
我的意思是，我对试镜记忆犹新，我记得我拿到角色的那一刻。

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.920
On how I met your mother or Good Morning Miami?
是《老爸老妈浪漫史》还是《晨安，迈阿密》？

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.040
No, on how I met your mother.
不，是《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.399
I remember it so well.
我记得太清楚了。

00:05:01.639 --> 00:05:07.399
And I remember coming in and being absolutely terrified of a multi-cam format.
我记得我走进片场时，对多机位格式感到绝对的恐惧。

00:05:07.399 --> 00:05:22.040
And I remember day one, you all setting the tone, which was this kind, all-inclusive, like first thing out of the gate is we finished the table read and we all went straight to breakfast.
我还记得第一天，你们所有人都定下了基调，那是一种善良的、包容的氛围，比如我们完成围读后的第一件事就是直奔早餐。

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:25.240
And it was all under the, you know, guidance of Pam Fryman.
这一切都是在帕姆·弗雷曼的指导下进行的。

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:33.360
Like it was a very, it was a very like, you're safe here, everything's okay, kind of vibe, which I definitely did not trust.
就像是一种，在这里你是安全的，一切都很好的氛围，但我绝对不相信。

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:36.560
I was like, sure, sure, we'll see what happens on tape night.
当时我想，真的假的，录制之夜再看吧。

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.500
You know, it was like my mentality was like, well, we'll see.
你知道的，我的心态就是，好吧，走着瞧吧。

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.579
It's a tape three days, which, yeah, you might not have known coming in, yeah.
那是三天录制期，是的，你刚来的时候可能不知道，是的。

00:05:43.579 --> 00:05:44.420
I didn't.
我确实不知道。

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:48.300
And I also, then was like, as soon as you were like, no, no, no, it's different around here.
而且我还以为，一旦你们说，不，不，不，这里情况不一样。

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.740
I was like, well, I'm definitely gonna get fired after the network run through.
我就想，好吧，网台试播集演完我肯定会被炒鱿鱼的。

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.740
Did you really feel that?
你当时真的这么觉得吗？

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:53.779
Oh, yeah, big time.
哦，是的，非常强烈。

00:05:53.779 --> 00:05:56.699
Because that was the culture I came from on Good Morning Miami.
因为那是我在《晨安，迈阿密》经历的文化。

00:05:56.699 --> 00:06:01.899
People were replaced left and right after, you know, table reads after run through is all that.
你知道的，在围读、试演之后，大家总是动不动就被换掉。

00:06:01.899 --> 00:06:11.899
So in so many ways, the show was this healing salve for my soul, you know, my multi-camera wounds, yeah.
所以在很多方面，这部剧就像是我心灵的治愈药膏，你知道的，治愈了我对多机位拍摄的创伤，是的。

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.899
And that was a good morning, Miami was like a live studio audience, like high pressure.
《晨安，迈阿密》就像是一个有现场观众的节目，压力很大。

00:06:16.899 --> 00:06:21.019
Like we have a big, that changes the vibe so much, I think.
就像我们有很多观众，我认为这极大地改变了氛围。

00:06:21.019 --> 00:06:30.980
I do have a very strong memory, actually, of watching James Burroughs, who was directing and watching him not watch the monitors, but snap his fingers.
实际上，我确实有一个非常深刻的记忆，就是看着詹姆斯·伯罗斯在导演，看着他不看监视器，而是打响指。

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:32.819
Like he's like, he was like a band leader.
就像他像个乐队指挥一样。

00:06:32.819 --> 00:06:35.180
He was like pacing the show.
他在掌控节目的节奏。

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:47.259
Which was such a great education in comedy because he taught me about the musicality of serving up the joke and all of that, which I truly like didn't, from theater, it was a little bit more organic, you know?
这真是喜剧的一堂生动的教育课，因为他教会了我抖包袱的音乐感以及诸如此类的事情，说实话我以前并不懂，从戏剧的角度来看，它会更自然一点，你懂吗？

00:06:47.259 --> 00:06:50.620
But this was, serve it and serve it hard and land your jokes.
但这个是，抛出包袱，狠狠地抛，让你的笑话落地。

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:55.740
And if you don't, somebody's gonna come talk to you and be like, this is not working.
如果你做不到，就会有人来找你，对你说，这样行不通。

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.300
Yeah, but you know, it's an interesting thing.
对，但你知道，这是一件很有趣的事情。

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.579
Like I always, maybe you share this.
就像我一直以来的感受一样，也许你也有同感。

00:06:59.579 --> 00:07:20.620
I always love working with older actors because they have a level of like relaxation and not giving a shit that is so enviable when you're younger, you're like, how do you get to that place where you're just like so relaxed, the jokes, you're not even, you don't look like you're trying, you look like you're just thinking about your sandwich, you're gonna have for lunch and it's endlessly watchable and captivating.
我总是很喜欢和资深演员合作，因为他们有一种放松的状态，有一种“老子不在乎”的松弛感，当你年轻的时候，你会无比羡慕，你会想：你是怎么做到这么放松的？那些笑话，你甚至都不用……你看上去根本没在刻意努力，你看上去只是在盘算午饭要吃三明治，而他们的表演却有着无穷的观赏性和吸引力。

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:26.779
There's something about being a new actor and especially, you know, I think because we We both went to theater school.
做新演员确实有某种特殊的体验，特别是，你知道的，我觉得因为我们俩都上过戏剧学校。

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:27.779
You went to Carnegie.
你上的是卡耐基。

00:07:27.779 --> 00:07:28.779
No, you went to BU, right?
不，你上的是波士顿大学，对吧？

00:07:28.779 --> 00:07:29.779
I went to BU.
我上的是波士顿大学。

00:07:29.779 --> 00:07:32.180
My husband went to Carnegie Mellon, yeah.
我丈夫上的是卡耐基梅隆，对。

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.899
And I went to NYU, and I felt like I was trained for theater jobs.
我上的是纽约大学，我当时觉得我受过训练，就是为了演戏剧。

00:07:35.899 --> 00:07:40.300
I knew how to get a script, I knew how to do the rehearsal, I knew how to be in the theater.
我知道怎么拿剧本，我知道怎么排练，我知道怎么在剧院里演戏。

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:45.100
They do not teach you how to be on a set of a TV show, of a movie.
但他们根本不教你怎么在电视剧或电影片场演戏。

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.860
You are really thrown in a deep end.
你真的是被直接扔进了深水区。

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:52.540
I remember Andre Brouwer came and talked to us, and he's like, do you know what the tape on the floor means?
我记得安德鲁·布劳尔来跟我们交流过，他说，你们知道地板上的胶带是什么意思吗？

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:55.314
such a language of a set that you have to figure out.
片场有太多你必须去摸索的“行话”和规矩。

00:07:55.314 --> 00:08:06.516
And if you're good enough to get cast or you're lucky enough to get cast and often both, you are really thrown into the, you're just like tossed off the boat and you're like, you better learn how to swim, you know?
如果你足够优秀能被选中，或者你足够幸运能被选中，通常这两者兼有，你真的就会被扔进……你就像是被直接从船上抛了下去，然后有人对你说：“最好快学会怎么游泳”，你知道吗？

00:08:06.516 --> 00:08:09.500
But you have to really, you have to really pay attention.
但你真的必须，你必须全神贯注。

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:20.871
Yeah, I also think like for those of us trained in theater, which truly I thought I was going to be doing regional theater in Ashland, Oregon for the rest of like, I, my agent was like, come for pilot season.
对，我也觉得，对于我们这些受过戏剧训练的人来说——真的，我以前以为我会在俄勒冈州阿什拉夫的地区剧院演一辈子戏，我的经纪人却对我说：“来试镜季看看吧。”

00:08:20.871 --> 00:08:23.167
And I was like, it's not going to go well.
当时我还想：这肯定不会顺利的。

00:08:23.167 --> 00:09:00.780
